--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Lazy-wave power cable restrained in torsion, deck mesh too coarse at touchdown
-- A finite-EI lazy-wave cable clamped at both ends and restrained in torsion (Rigid, zero
-- pretwist), so its static solve runs in 3D. The deck mesh is 4 m up to the end of the
-- buoyancy section and 10 m along the grounded run, longer than half the bending length
-- (EI/w)^(1/3) = 5.0 m of the bare cable. On that mesh the pointwise axial resultant of the
-- under-resolved touchdown elements oscillates into compression at Gauss points, and the
-- tangent of the stable equilibrium shows a spurious out-of-plane negative eigenvalue there.
-- The static solve repeats the route on the refined mesh, which is stable, and reports it once.
